 "protocol": {
  "source": "preset",
  "text": "Elephant toothpaste, the standard bench demo. The flask already holds the dish soap and food colouring.\n\n1. Put the empty beaker P1 on the scale and pour 39 g of the 12 % hydrogen peroxide developer into it (within 2 g).\n2. Pour P1 into the flask through the funnel, then put P1 back in the carousel.\n3. Dose one packet of instant yeast, about 7 g (within 0.7 g, at most two top-ups), into P2 with the auger.\n4. Bring P2 to the scale and check the yeast weight.\n5. Add 30 g of warm water on top of the yeast (within 2 g) and let it activate for 60 seconds.\n6. Pour the yeast slurry into the flask and move the stage to ERUPT as soon as the pourer is clear, then put P2 back in the carousel.\n",
  "steps": [
   {
    "type": "TRANSFER",
    "params": {
     "beaker": "P1",
     "src": "carousel_pick",
     "dst": "scale_pan"
    },
